  "body": "### Summary\n\nCapture on the Mac, with the LOT-001 (#38) kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), the page state: A message whose quote or edit link is printed in clear (an `<a href>` wrapper, or a path in the class) instead of the obfuscated `md_noclass_cryptlink<hex>` class.\n\n### Scope\n\nState to capture: A message whose quote or edit link is printed in clear (an `<a href>` wrapper, or a path in the class) instead of the obfuscated `md_noclass_cryptlink<hex>` class.\n\nNote: legacy and the LOT-031 parser read only the wrapper's `class`; a clear `<a href>` gives nil until a capture shows the shape. May not exist on today's HFR: record it if never seen\n\nRules: anonymize every free-text field; never hand-build the state in the cloud (LESSONS 36); add a legacy oracle when a parser consumes it (LOT-002 (#39)..005 tooling); one PR per batch of captures.\n\n### Wanted by\n\nLOT-031 (#58), spec `docs/lots/LOT-031-message-actions.md` \"Pending capture\" (PR #28)\n\n### Depends on\n\n—\n\n### Owner / session\n\n— (ready; `host: mac`)\n\n### Source\n\nPending capture listed by LOT-031 (PR #28).\n",
